{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-256", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/256", "wordCount": 702, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hi. I'm Neha Agrawal, and I'm"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "a software engineer working on"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "speech recognition."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "In 2016, we introduced the"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "Speech Recognition framework for"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "developers to solve their speech"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "recognition needs."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "For anyone who is new to this"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "framework, I highly recommend"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "watching this Speech Recognition"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "API session by my colleague"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "Henry Mason."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "In this video, we're going to"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "discuss exciting new advances in"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "the APIs. Let's get started."}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "Speech recognition is now"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "supported for macOS."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "The support is available for"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "both AppKit and iPad apps on"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "Mac."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "Just like iOS, over 50 languages"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "are supported."}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "You need approval from your"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "users to access the microphone"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "and record their speech, and"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "they also need to have Siri"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "enabled."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "In addition to supporting speech"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "recognition on macOS, we are now"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "allowing developers to run"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "recognition on-device for"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "privacy sensitive applications."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "With on-device support, your"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "user's data will not be sent to"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "Apple servers."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "Your app no longer needs to rely"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "on a network connection, and"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "cellular data will not be"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "consumed."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "However, there are tradeoffs to"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "consider."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Accuracy is good on-device, but"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "you may find it is better on"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "server due to a continuous"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "learning."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "A server-based recognition"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "support has limits on number of"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "requests and audio duration."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "With on-device recognition,"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "these limits do not apply."}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "The number of languages"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "supported on server are more"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "than on-device."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Also, if server isn't available,"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "our server mode automatically"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "falls back on on-device"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "recognition if it is supported."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "All iPhones and iPads with Apple"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "A9 or later processors are"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "supported, and all Mac devices"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "are supported."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "There are over 10 languages"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "supported for on-device"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "recognition."}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "Now, let's look at how to enable"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "on-device recognition in code."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "To recognize pre-recorded audio,"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "we first create an"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "SFSpeechRecognizer object and"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "check for availability of speech"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "recognition on that object."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "If speech recognition is"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "available, we can create a"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "recognition request with the"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "audio file URL and start"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "recognition."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "Now, in order to use on-device"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "recognition, you need to first"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "check if on-device recognition"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "is supported and then set"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "requiresOnDeviceRecognition"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "property on the request object."}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "Now that we have looked at this"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "in code, let's talk about the"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "results you get."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "Since iOS 10 in speech"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "recognition results, we have"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "provided transcriptions,"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "alternative interpretations,"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "confidence levels and timing"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "We're making a few more"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "additions to the speech"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "recognition results."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "Speaking rate measures how fast"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "a person speaks in words per"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "minute."}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "Average pause duration measures"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "the average length of pause"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "between words."}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "And voice analytics features"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "include various measures of"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "vocal characteristics."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "Now, voice analytics gives"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "insight into four features."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "Jitter measures how pitch varies"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "in audio."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "With voice analytics, you can"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "now understand the amount of"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "jitter in speech expressed as a"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "percentage."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "Shimmer measures how amplitude"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "varies in audio, and with voice"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "analytics, you can understand"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "shimmer in speech expressed in"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "decibels."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Let's listen to some audio"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "samples to understand what"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "speech with high jitter and"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "shimmer sounds like."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "First, let's hear audio with"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "normal speech."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "Apple."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "Now, audio with perturbed"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "speech."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Apple."}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "Next feature is pitch."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "Pitch measures the highness and"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "lowness of the tone."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "Often, women and children have"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "higher pitch."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "And voicing is used to identify"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "voiced regions in speech."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "The voice analytics features are"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "specific to an individual, and"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "they can vary with time and"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "circumstances."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "For example, if the person is"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "tired, these features will be"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "different than when they're not."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Also, depending on who the"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "person is talking to, these"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "features may vary."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "These new results are part of"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "the SF transcription object and"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "will be available periodically."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "We will have them at the end"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "when the isFinal flag is sent,"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "but we could also see them"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "before."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "You can access speakingRate and"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "averagePauseDuration as shown."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "To access voice analytics, you"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "would have to access the SF"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "transcription segment object,"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "and then you can access it as"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "shown here."}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "To summarize, we have made three"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "key advances."}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "You can now build apps on macOS"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "using speech recognition APIs."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "Speech recognition can be run"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "on-device in a privacy-friendly"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "manner."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "And you now have access to voice"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "analytics features for getting"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "insight into vocal"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "characteristics."}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "For more information, check out"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "the session's web page and"}]}
